var e=`July 20 • July 27 • August 3 • August 10 • August 16`,t=`Śrāvaṇa Somavāra = The Most Powerful Day to Please Bhagavān Śiva`,n=`Śrāvaṇa Somavāra is traditionally regarded as an especially sacred time for Śiva worship. Devotees observe Śiva Ārādhana, Jalābhiṣeka, mantra japa, fasting and acts of dāna as part of their spiritual practice during the sacred month of Śrāvaṇa.`,r=[{num:`01`,title:`Śiva’s Favorite Month`,source:`Śiva Purāṇa · Koṭi Rudra Saṁhitā`,text:`Śrāvaṇa is traditionally regarded as especially dear to Śiva. The sacred tradition connects this month with Śiva’s protection of the world during the Samudra Manthana and His acceptance of the Hālāhala poison.`},{num:`02`,title:`Pārvatī’s Tapas`,source:`Skanda Purāṇa`,text:`Goddess Pārvatī is traditionally described as performing intense tapas to attain Śiva. Śrāvaṇa Somavāra is therefore associated with devotion, vrata and prayer.`},{num:`03`,title:`Samudra Manthana`,source:`Bhāgavata Purāṇa 8.7`,text:`During the churning of the cosmic ocean, Śiva accepted the Hālāhala poison. Devotional traditions therefore emphasize water offerings and Jalābhiṣeka during Śrāvaṇa.`},{num:`04`,title:`Cāturmāsya`,source:`Padma Purāṇa`,text:`Śrāvaṇa falls within the sacred Cāturmāsya period, traditionally associated with increased devotion, vrata, dāna and spiritual discipline.`},{num:`05`,title:`Śiva Sannidhya`,source:`Traditional Teaching`,text:`Śrāvaṇa is traditionally regarded as a particularly auspicious period for Śiva worship and spiritual practice.`}],i={heading:`Tantra Śāstra Reason`,body:`Traditional Śaiva and Tantric practices associate Śrāvaṇa with the water element and Śiva worship. Water Abhiṣeka is traditionally understood as a cooling and purifying devotional practice. Monday is associated with Chandra, and Chandra is traditionally depicted upon Śiva’s head. Therefore, Somavāra worship is associated with peace, mental steadiness and devotion.`},a=[{num:`01`,title:`Turanta Phala`,text:`Traditional texts describe Śrāvaṇa Somavāra worship as especially auspicious and spiritually fruitful.`},{num:`02`,title:`Karma Dahaka`,text:`Śiva worship and Somavāra vrata are traditionally associated with purification, discipline and release from accumulated karmic burdens.`},{num:`03`,title:`Manokāmanā Pūrti`,text:`The vrata is traditionally associated with sincere prayer for family well-being, marriage, prosperity, spiritual progress and fulfillment of righteous aspirations.`}],o={transliteration:`“Śrāvaṇe śaṅkaraṁ pūjya somavāre viśeṣataḥ | Yaḥ karoti naraḥ bhaktyā sa yāti śiva-sāyujyam ||”`,meaning:`One who worships Śiva with devotion on Śrāvaṇa Monday is traditionally praised as attaining spiritual closeness and union with Śiva.`},s=`Abhiṣeka is the devotional practice of bathing the Śiva Liṅga with sacred substances known as dravyas.`,c=[{num:`01`,name:`Jala`,detail:`Water — traditionally associated with cooling and calming qualities in Śiva worship.`,body:`Traditional association: peace of mind and cooling purification.`},{num:`02`,name:`Dūdha / Milk`,detail:`Traditional association: health, nourishment and prosperity.`,body:null},{num:`03`,name:`Dahi / Curd`,detail:`Traditional association: stability, family well-being and auspiciousness.`,body:null},{num:`04`,name:`Ghee`,detail:`Traditional association: tejas, prosperity, recognition and auspiciousness.`,body:null},{num:`05`,name:`Madhu / Honey`,detail:`Traditional association: sweet speech, harmony and auspicious communication.`,body:null},{num:`06`,name:`Sugar / Jaggery`,detail:`Traditional association: happiness, sweetness and harmony in relationships.`,body:null},{num:`07`,name:`Pañcāmṛta`,detail:`A traditional combination of sacred substances and an important offering in many forms of Hindu worship.`,body:null},{num:`08`,name:`Coconut Water`,detail:`Traditional association: fertility, nourishment and family well-being.`,body:null},{num:`09`,name:`Bilva Jala`,detail:`Bilva leaves are especially sacred in Śiva worship. The three leaflets are traditionally associated with sacred triads including the Trimūrti.`,body:null},{num:`10`,name:`Gaṅgā Jala`,detail:`Sacred Gaṅgā water is traditionally associated with purification and spiritual merit.`,body:null},{num:`11`,name:`Rudrābhiṣeka`,detail:`A special form of Śiva worship involving Rudra mantras and Abhiṣeka. Traditionally performed with devotion, discipline and mantra recitation.`,body:null}],l=[{num:`01`,name:`Roga Nāśa`,text:`Traditional prayers for health, purification and well-being.`},{num:`02`,name:`Ṛṇa + Daridra Nāśa`,text:`Traditional prayers for relief from financial difficulties and cultivation of responsible prosperity.`},{num:`03`,name:`Graha Śānti`,text:`Śiva worship is traditionally associated with peace and spiritual remedies connected with planetary influences.`},{num:`04`,name:`Kāla Sarpa + Pitṛ Doṣa`,text:`Certain Śaiva traditions associate specific Abhiṣeka practices with prayers for relief from perceived spiritual or ancestral difficulties.`},{num:`05`,name:`Santāna Prāpti`,text:`Traditional prayers for family growth, fertility and children.`},{num:`06`,name:`Vivāha Sukha`,text:`Somavāra vrata is traditionally associated with prayers for a harmonious marriage and family life.`},{num:`07`,name:`Śatru Nāśa`,text:`Rudra worship is traditionally associated with overcoming obstacles and cultivating inner strength.`},{num:`08`,name:`Mokṣa`,text:`Śiva worship ultimately points toward spiritual liberation and devotion to the Divine.`}],u=`These benefits are presented as traditional spiritual beliefs and devotional aspirations, not guaranteed medical, financial or supernatural results.`,d={heading:`Tantra Secret / Mantra Practice`,body:`During Abhiṣeka, devotees may traditionally recite the Mahāmṛtyuñjaya Mantra or appropriate Rudra mantras according to their sampradāya, guru or temple tradition. Do not present supernatural results as guaranteed.`},f=[{step:1,title:`Preparation`,points:[`Observe fasting or take suitable fruits according to your health and tradition.`,`Wear clean clothes, traditionally white where appropriate.`,`Prepare the worship space.`]},{step:2,title:`Abhiṣeka — 11 Minutes`,points:[`Begin with water Abhiṣeka while chanting an appropriate Śiva or Rudra mantra.`,`Then offer milk if it is part of your tradition, followed by water.`,`Offer: Bilva leaves, Dhattūra where traditionally appropriate, white flowers, suitable naivedya.`]},{step:3,title:`Mantra + Dhyāna`,points:[`Chant the Śiva Mantra — 108 times, or recite Rudrāṣṭakam.`,`Meditate upon Śiva with the crescent moon upon His head.`]},{step:4,title:`Prasāda + Dāna`,points:[`Distribute prasāda.`,`Traditional Monday dāna may include: black sesame, rice, white cloth, food according to one’s ability.`]}],p=[{num:`01`,name:`Bilva`,text:`Bilva leaves are especially sacred in Śiva worship.`},{num:`02`,name:`Fasting`,text:`Those observing a fast may traditionally choose fruits, milk or other permitted foods according to their health and family tradition.`},{num:`03`,name:`Personal Discipline`,text:`Maintain cleanliness, simplicity and devotional discipline.`},{num:`04`,name:`Pañcākṣarī Mantra`,text:`Chant Na-Ma-Śi-Vā-Ya while performing water Abhiṣeka.`},{num:`05`,name:`Five Mondays`,text:`Devotees may observe the practice across the Śrāvaṇa Mondays according to their family or sampradāya tradition.`}],m=[{label:`Purāṇa`,text:`Śiva Purāṇa traditions emphasize the special devotional importance of Śrāvaṇa and Somavāra worship.`},{label:`Tantra`,text:`Śaiva and Tantric traditions emphasize Abhiṣeka, mantra, meditation and elemental symbolism.`},{label:`Result`,text:`The deeper purpose of Śrāvaṇa Somavāra is devotion, discipline, inner purification and surrender to Śiva.`}],h=`“In Śrāvaṇa, don’t just ask Śiva for things. Pour your ego like water on the Liṅga. He will return peace.”`,g=`This is a devotional/editorial message, not a direct scriptural quotation.`,_=[`Śiva Purāṇa · Koṭi Rudra Saṁhitā`,`Skanda Purāṇa`,`Bhāgavata Purāṇa 8.7`,`Padma Purāṇa`,`Śaiva Āgama Traditions`,`Rudra Mantra Parampara`];export{t as _,m as a,h as c,d,f,_ as g,o as h,c as i,g as l,p as m,s as n,a as o,r as p,u as r,e as s,l as t,n as u,i as v};